ion markets give Ford roughly a one-in-five chance.\n\nPublic polling is sparse and comes only from Democratic-sponsored firms, but it shows a narrow race: Spartz led by two points in July and by one in early October. A favorable national midterm climate for Democrats appears to have eaten into the district's usual Republican margin, yet incumbency, the district's lean, and Spartz's money advantage keep her favored. The race lands in Lean Republican territory, tighter than most raters suggest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1386, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1359, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1346, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1196, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1263, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1331, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1305, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1313, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1321, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1281, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1641, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1655, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1058, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1258, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.1311, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.1757, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.1048, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.2027, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.1615, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.1641, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.0969, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.0935, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-17", "p_dem": 0.1441, "margin": -6.5}, {"da